trajectory.patch:
The linker errors indicate that the DAC emulator driver is not being compiled and linked into the final application. This is due to an incorrect Kconfig dependency that disables the driver when a corresponding devicetree node is present. Additionally, one of the devicetree nodes used in the test is missing its `compatible` property, which would cause a linker error even after the Kconfig issue is resolved.

Here are the fixes:

1.  Correct the Kconfig dependency for the DAC emulator driver to enable it when a `zephyr,dac-emul` compatible node is present in the devicetree.
2.  Add the missing `compatible = "zephyr,dac-emul";` property to the `dac_emul0` node in the test overlay file.

drivers/dac/Kconfig.dac_emul
<<<<<<<< SEARCH
config DAC_EMUL
	bool "DAC emulator"
	default y
	depends on !DT_HAS_ZEPHYR_DAC_EMUL_ENABLED
========
config DAC_EMUL
	bool "DAC emulator"
	depends on DT_HAS_ZEPHYR_DAC_EMUL_ENABLED
>>>>>>>> REPLACE
tests/drivers/dac/dac_emul/boards/native_sim.overlay
<<<<<<<< SEARCH
	dac_emul0: dac-emulator-0 {
		nchannels = <4>;
		#io-channel-cells = <1>;
		status = "okay";
	};
========
	dac_emul0: dac-emulator-0 {
		compatible = "zephyr,dac-emul";
		nchannels = <4>;
		#io-channel-cells = <1>;
		status = "okay";
	};
>>>>>>>> REPLACE
